--- /dev/null
+++ b/downstream/ORIGINAL_SOURCE_POSITIONS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Preserve original positions through paragraph and table transformations
+
+This narrow owner investigation starts at Swift cmark0.8.0 commit
+924936d0427cb25a61169739a7660230bffa6ea6. It must correct source metadata while
+preserving parsed/rendered document semantics and the existing public C API.
+No application pin may adopt an unqualified candidate.
+
+Reproduced defects: a paragraph before a table loses its source positions and
+header cells retain concatenated-buffer offsets on the preceding line; inline
+nodes on a continuation line retain the first line's indentation even when the
+actual quote/list indentation differs or the line is a lazy continuation.
+
+Record sparse content-offset to original line/byte-column segments as block
+content is appended. Include offset changes from partially consumed tabs,
+reference-definition removal and table paragraph/header/cell extraction plus
+escaped-pipe removal. Store metadata with the existing opaque node, free it
+with its allocator, and keep absent metadata compatible with manually built
+nodes. This is internal node layout, not a change to the public opaque-node API.
+
+Keep inline parsing and delimiter/reference algorithms unchanged. After inline
+parsing finishes, map legacy relative coordinates through the recorded content
+segments; accounting for multiline inline-code/HTML endpoints must be explicit.
+Never let corrected coordinates alter calculations while the parser is still
+using them for delimiter or reference semantics. Table split nodes must receive
+both block coordinates and copied source mappings before inline processing.
+
+Qualification must use actual Swift Markdown plus cmark, explicit Unicode,
+CRLF/CR/LF, indentation/lazy continuations, tabs, multiline code/HTML, escaped
+pipes, links/reference definitions and paragraph/table header/body cases. Keep
+all failing-before evidence. Compare original/candidate parsed non-position
+structure and rendered bytes on a generated corpus, run the original C and
+Swift Markdown tests, sanitizers and the exact MarkdownEngine fixture. Fix
+incorrect coordinate expectations only against original authored-byte oracles;
+never loosen bounds or omit failing cases. Preserve original licenses, exact
+base/source manifests and all unrelated package identities.
