@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Qualification of original source coordinates
+
+Only five runtime files change from the exact Swift cmark0.8.0 source recorded
+in source-position-patch.json. All other original tracked files, public C header,
+package manifest and complete COPYING remain byte-identical. The internal opaque
+node layout gains sparse provenance; the public opaque-node API is unchanged.
+Each changed file carries a prominent downstream modification notice.
+
+The unchanged runtime fails53 coordinate assertions on Unicode, LF/CRLF/CR,
+variable/lazy container prefixes, paragraph/table splitting, removed reference
+definitions, multiline code/HTML and escaped table pipes. The candidate passes
+those controls and an additional authored closing-brace oracle. The complete
+Swift Markdown suite passes299 XCTest and6 new Swift Testing functions in Debug
+and Release. Its one pre-existing snapshot expected a closing brace at column3
+although the authored byte is column1; the direct byte-range oracle proves the
+corrected expectation. Initial failures remain in the application evidence.
+
+Original C API668 controls pass normally, with AddressSanitizer and with
+UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. Exact unnormalized reference outputs pass670 CommonMark,
+26 regression,30 GFM and16 smart punctuation cases using their original setup.
+A first extension invocation omitted required extension flags and failed27 cases;
+that setup failure is retained, then the exact CMake-configured invocation passes.
+
+The actual Swift Markdown original/candidate AST content and formatted Markdown
+are identical for9054 deterministic generated cases. Actual HTML parsing enables
+source positions in both runtimes; removing only generated numeric data-sourcepos
+attributes leaves every other rendered byte identical for all9054 sources. Raw
+position attributes change in54 cases. An AddressSanitizer execution produces
+identical complete AST/format outputs for the same9054 inputs, with no finding.
+The actual application MarkdownEngine source and all158 tests pass Debug/Release
+against this owner, including queue/cancellation/YAML/depth/block/source/timing
+controls and new exact continuation/table assertions. No native product executes.
+
+This is qualification of parser metadata, not upstream acceptance, production
+math activation, native UI/VoiceOver or the whole-editor1MiB/50ms budget. Application
+integration still requires exact immutable pins, retained notices/manifest and
+complete exact-head hosted CI. Original failed and corrected test logs are
+identified by digest; full receipts are retained with the application change.
